---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = "Designing an RFI-to-Enrolled journey — Code to Click";
const description = "How to design the full Higher Ed enrollment marketing lifecycle in Marketing Cloud — from RFI capture through yield and melt mitigation.";
---
<Base title={title} description={description}>
<section class="phero">
  <div class="wrap" style="padding-bottom:52px">
    <div class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/insights">Insights</a> / Higher Education</div>
    <span class="eyebrow kick">Higher Education</span>
    <h1>Designing an <span class="g">RFI-to-Enrolled</span> journey</h1>
    <div class="meta" style="color:#8FA0C4;font-family:'IBM Plex Mono';font-size:12px;margin-top:16px;display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap"><span>The Code to Click Team</span><span>6 min read</span><span>Higher Education</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="article prose reveal">
      <p class="lead">Enrollment marketing isn't one campaign &mdash; it's a funnel. The schools that win treat each stage as its own journey, with the right message at the right moment, all the way from a first inquiry to a deposited, enrolled student.</p>

      <h2>Map the funnel first</h2>
      <p>Before building anything in Marketing Cloud, agree on the stages and the trigger that moves a prospect between them:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Inquiry (RFI)</strong> &mdash; a prospect requests information.</li>
        <li><strong>Prospect nurture</strong> &mdash; warming inquiries and stealth prospects toward an application.</li>
        <li><strong>Applicant</strong> &mdash; application started; the goal is completion.</li>
        <li><strong>Admit / Yield</strong> &mdash; admitted; the goal is a deposit and enrollment.</li>
        <li><strong>Melt</strong> &mdash; committed but not yet enrolled; keep them engaged through summer.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Design journey by journey</h2>
      <p>Each stage becomes a Journey Builder flow with its own entry criteria, cadence and exit. A few principles carry across all of them:</p>
      <h3>Start the RFI journey fast</h3>
      <p>Speed-to-first-touch matters. An RFI should trigger an immediate, helpful response &mdash; program details, next steps, a clear call to apply or talk to an advisor &mdash; then settle into a nurture cadence tuned to the prospect's program and timeline.</p>
      <h3>Make the application journey remove friction</h3>
      <p>Applicants abandon. Sequenced nudges, deadline reminders, and "you're almost there" prompts &mdash; personalized to where they are in the application &mdash; recover starts that would otherwise be lost.</p>
      <h3>Treat yield and melt as distinct</h3>
      <p>Converting an admit to a deposit is a different job than keeping a committed student engaged through the summer. Separate the two: a yield journey that sells the fit and the outcome, and a melt-mitigation journey that stays warm with orientation, community and logistics.</p>

      <h2>Data and triggers</h2>
      <p>The journeys are only as smart as the data behind them. Application status, program interest, event attendance and advisor interactions should drive entry and branching &mdash; ideally unified on <strong>Data 360</strong> and connected to Education Cloud so marketing, admissions and advising work from the same picture.</p>

      <h2>Personalize on three axes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Program</strong> &mdash; a nursing prospect and an MBA prospect want different things.</li>
        <li><strong>Stage</strong> &mdash; message to where they are in the funnel, not where you wish they were.</li>
        <li><strong>Persona</strong> &mdash; first-year, transfer, graduate and adult learners follow different paths.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Measure what matters</h2>
      <p>Report on stage-to-stage conversion, not just opens and clicks. RFI-to-application, application-to-complete, admit-to-deposit and melt rate are the numbers that tell you the funnel is actually moving.</p>

      <div class="postnav">
        <a class="arrow" href="/insights">&larr; All insights</a>
        <a class="arrow" href="/industries#higher-ed">Higher Education at Code to Click &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="blk alt" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:56px"><div class="wrap"><div class="ctaband reveal">
  <h2>Want the enrollment funnel built right?</h2>
  <p>We bring a ready-to-tailor Higher Ed journey library to the first workshop.</p>
  <div class="cta"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">Book a consult &rarr;</a><a class="btn btn-light" href="/marketing-cloud#journeys">See the journeys</a></div>
</div></div></section>
</Base>
